## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop**: One `Game` state object; `mulberry32(seed)` feeds all randomness (terrain, colonists, ashstorm, events, trade); `endTurn()` resolves 10 steps in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map**: 8x8 `this.map` built with `generateTerrain(this.rng,...)`; `canBuild` checks `building.terrain.includes(tile.terrain)`; `adjacency_bonus` multiplies `produce` in `produceResources()`. Score 2.

**F3 — Economy**: `conversions` chains ore→metal, ash→soil→food in `produceResources()`; total-resource cap vs `storage_capacity` with overflow drop loop. Score 2.

**F4 — Population**: colonists have name/job/skills/fatigue/morale; `skill_bonus = c.skills[building.skill]` read by production, but `fatigue` is only incremented/decayed, never read by production or any decision logic. Score 1.

**F5 — Needs**: consumption `-1 food/water` per colonist; shortage triggers `morale -=5`; recovery via events/production morale gains — but morale is never read back into the production formula (`produceResources` has no morale factor). Score 1.

**F6 — Research**: 8 nodes in `RESEARCH_TREE`; `canResearch` enforces prereqs+cost; only 4/8 nodes (`ore_refining`,`irrigation`,`power_grid`,`shelter_tech`) apply any effect in `doResearch`, the rest (advanced_forge, soil_science, preservation, advanced_lab) do nothing. Score 1.

**F7 — Events**: 10 entries in `EVENTS`; weighted pick + cooldown in `fireEvent`; 4 events have 2 outcomes, but outcome is chosen by `Math.floor(this.rng()*...)`, not the player — no real "choice" UI exists. Score 1.

**F8 — Trade**: `updateTradeState()` sets prices from `trade_supply` drift + stockpile check; `buyResource`/`sellResource` both work, but no caravan inventory cap — buy/sell unlimited any turn. Score 1.

**F9 — Hazard**: `triggerAshstorm` fires periodically, damages `tile.building_health`, read by `health_factor` in production; `storm_damage_reduction` reduced via `shelter_tech`; but no repair function exists anywhere — building_health never increases. Score 1.

**F10 — Save/load**: `serialize()`/`Game.deserialize()` round-trip via textarea; `loadGame()` catches parse errors and `alert`s; some fields (event_log, trade_supply) omitted from serialize. Score 2.

**F11 — End conditions**: win check (`turn>=60 && pop>=12 && food/water>=20`) and lose check (`colonists.length===0`) both reachable in `endTurn`; `calculateScore()` combines pop/research/scrip/turn; `renderGameOverModal()` shown. Score 2.

**F12 — UI**: `switchTab`, log entries carry `entry.turn`, keyboard `1-6`/Space wired, `@media (max-width:600px)` responsive layout — but tooltips (`title=`) only describe building purpose, not numeric derivation of stats. Score 1.

**F13 — Dev panel**: `runTests()` checks real invariants (save/load round-trip, cooldowns, prereqs); `runBenchmark()` clones state, runs 200 headless turns, prints `state_hash`. Score 2.

**G1**: `doResearch` grants one-time resource bumps (`resources.ore += 5`) instead of storing a yield modifier; `produceResources()` never reads `research_done`. Score 0.

**G2**: food/water shortfall → `colonists.forEach(c => c.morale -= 5)` real state change, but morale never enters the production formula in `produceResources()`. Score 1.

**G3**: `triggerAshstorm` sets `tile.building_health`, read by `health_factor` in `produceResources` (real output loss); no repair function anywhere restores `building_health`. Score 2.

**G4**: `updateTradeState()` reads `trade_supply` drift and `this.resources[res]>200` threshold into `trade_prices`, applied on caravan cycles, displayed in Trade tab. Score 3.

**G5**: `settler_arrival`/`equipment_malfunction` outcome branches write different resource/colonist mutations, but branch is RNG-selected (`Math.floor(this.rng()*outcomes.length)`), not a player choice. Score 3.

